{
  "description": "Webhook signature contract shared by the Python (ab0t-quota) and Go (ab0t-quota-go) receivers; identical copies in both repositories. Standard Webhooks (the auth service's webhook-* headers): key = base64-decode(secret minus 'whsec_') when valid padded standard base64 (CR/LF ignored), else the secret's UTF-8 bytes; webhook-signature = space-separated 'v1,<base64 HMAC-SHA256(key, id.timestamp.body)>' tokens; webhook-timestamp = ASCII digits only (1-15); accept iff |now - timestamp| <= tolerance_seconds and any v1 token matches any configured non-empty secret. Order: timestamp syntax, tolerance, signature. 'now' is decimal seconds. Legacy X-Event-Signature: HMAC-SHA256(secret bytes, body) as 'sha256=<hex>' or '<hex>', hex case-insensitive, nothing else.",
